abduco
Usage: abduco [-n|-c|-a] NAME [CMD...]

Keeps a shell -- or any program -- alive when you step away or get cut off.
Start a program inside a named session, detach, and it keeps running; attach
again later and it is exactly where you left it. On a stick you reach over a
tunnel, this is what survives a dropped connection.

	abduco               list the sessions that are running
	abduco -n NAME CMD   start CMD in a new session called NAME
	abduco -a NAME       attach -- step back into a running session
	ctrl-\               detach: step away, leaving it running

See also: dvtm, xexec
